['Here is a Python code using Flask framework for this web application. Flask is a lightweight and modular web application framework for developing Web applications. It's required to install via pip.

```python
from flask import Flask, redirect, request
import re

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/')
def index():
    return 'Hello World!'

@app.route('/redirect', methods=['GET'])
def redirection():
    target = request.args.get('target', default = "*")

    if re.search(r'example\.com', target):  # Regex pattern for 'example.com' in the URL
        return redirect(target)
    else:
        return redirect('/')

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run()
```
This code will start a web server and listen on localhost port 5000 by default. Visit http://localhost:5000/redirect?target=http://example.com to see it in action. Please replace the `'http://example.com'` with your desired URL that you want to redirect to.

In this code, we have created a route '/redirect' where 'target' parameter can be provided as a query string. The Flask request object is used to access these parameters. If the target matches our regex pattern (contains `example.com`) it will redirect to that URL else it will redirect to root URL '/'.

Make sure to replace `'http://example.com'` with your desired URL. Also, please remember to install Flask via pip if you haven't done so already by running `pip install flask` in the command line/terminal.
